ting here is risky because any Ace, King, spade, or medium pair beats me. My opponent will likely only call with hands that beat me and fold hands I'm already beating. This makes a bet -EV (negative expected value).\n\nChecking allows me to see showdown for free and potentially win against complete air or a weaker pair. It's the most prudent play given my weak holding and the uncertain strength of my opponent.\n\n**Answer:** 0"}
